{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1354495-brain-in-a-box","id":1354495,"title":"Brain in a Box","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-11T17:15:18-08:00","id":1354495,"title":"Brain in a Box","content":"How would you handle a character using super science or something to put their brain (possibly along with other organs they can't easily replace with machines) in a life supporting module which they attach to a drone or vehicle of some kind?<br /> <br /> I've just got this idea floating around and I'm not trying to narrow this down to just corebook modern Talent Inspired Super Science or Aeon Psion Biotech Super Science, or whatever. I'm more interested in how others would handle a character that has no real body in terms of physical Attributes (except maybe Stamina?) anymore. They are just a bunch of organs in a smallish box only interacting with things through tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T18:44:08-08:00","id":1354506,"title":"","content":"Check out the TC Mass Effect thread. There's stuff in there about Qin Bodysuits. Probably the best way would be to kludge something from that.<br /> <br /> If this is an NPC the Qin and maybe Aberrant stuff in Aeon might be sufficient. If this is a PC, honestly, I'd try to talk them out of it. The adventures/world is something that is pretty designed for humanoids. Two arms, Two legs, can see, hear, smell and touch. Having to constantly give special description of everything in the world for the Box-Brain is likely to get tiresome for you and any other players.<br /> <br /> That said, here's an adventure scenario dealing with something similar to that situation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://fabledlands.blogspot.com/2019/10/the-end-of-line-scenario.html#comment-form\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fabledlands.blogspot.com/2019/10/the-end-of-line-scenario.html#comment-form\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fabledlands.blogspot.com/2019/10/the-end-of-line-scenario.html#comment-form\" target=\"_blank\"> http://fabledlands.blogspot.com/2019/10/the-end-of-line-scenario.html#comment-form </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The scenario was originally written for GURPS in the Cthulhu By Gaslight setting, but it's all I've got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T10:37:19-08:00","id":1354607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1354495-brain-in-a-box?p=1354506#post1354506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having to constantly give special description of everything in the world for the Box-Brain is likely to get tiresome for you and any other players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why there would be any need for special description. The character wouldn't be seeing illusions like in that Cthulhu scenario. They would just be operating drones to interact with the world, potentially physically present (to prevent jamming cutting them off from the group) as a module inside a large-ish drone.<br /> <br /> Edit: They would still experience the world through sight and sound, through cameras and microphones not eyes and ears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 12-12-2019, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T11:31:12-08:00","id":1354626,"title":"","content":"I'd also suggest having a Persistent Condition of Head In a Box, so that any time that the fact that they are a Head In A Box causes them to fail or complicate a situation they get Momentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}